WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
Water, ice and steam.

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.030
A shamrock.

3
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.060
The sun, its light and its heat.

4
00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.970
These pictures are often
used for the Trinity.

5
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.430
Each one helps, and each one can mislead.

6
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:19.020
Around the year 400, Augustine looked for
a better picture inside the human mind.

7
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.180
So is God more like one mind
knowing and loving itself,

8
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:26.150
or three persons in perfect friendship?

9
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.670
In this mission, you'll
compare these pictures,

10
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.590
and what each one protects and risks.

11
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.160
Then you'll meet 2 modern theologians,
Karl Barth and Karl Rahner,

12
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.450
who start somewhere else entirely.

13
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.160
Your mission: weigh up how
Christians picture the Trinity,

14
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.120
and what each picture risks.
